1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
This is number 25.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Something's interfering with the transmission.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
That's going on.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
What's going on?

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
How is this happening?

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
What's happening?

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Haunt springs.

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Warm water that wells from the center of the earth.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
They have enchanted humans for ages.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
People flock from all over to soak their aching bodies in nature's scalding hot baths.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Healing, relaxing, and revitalizing.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
No one can resist their charms.

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:01:16,000
This is the wave

14
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:45,980
Thank you.

15
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:15,980
Thank you.

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,740
And I mean, we want the spirits to make discoveries and think for themselves, so I'll make the arrangements.

17
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,740
Besides, we want them happy, right?

18
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,040
No one likes an angry spirit.

19
00:02:25,340 --> 00:02:25,680
Right.

20
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:27,560
So, where are you going?

21
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:30,380
I was thinking Tekko Paradise since it's coming.

22
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:32,040
Yes, that's a great one.

23
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,180
Hey, listen, you should join them.

24
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,060
Give yourself a break.

25
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,020
I can take care of everything for you here.

26
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:39,700
You must think I'm crazy.

27
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,120
I absolutely do not.

28
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:44,480
I think you're working too hard and we can't function if our commander is exhausted.

29
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:45,800
So do us all a favor.

30
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,140
Go to the hot springs.

31
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:48,580
What are you really after?

32
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:50,420
I have no idea what you mean.

33
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,220
I have no desire to install several surveillance cameras there.

34
00:02:53,220 --> 00:03:00,840
Would someone like me actually fill a hot spring with lenses so that I could stare at every inch of that hard, tight, young body at my discretion?

35
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,440
Especially the back side.

36
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:07,340
No, no, not the internment camp.

37
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,260
Please have mercy.

38
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,500
Please forgive me, commander.

39
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:10,860
Anywhere but there, please.

40
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:12,400
Listen up, Kanazuki.

41
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:16,560
When you get to the camp, you're going to start digging a hole and not stop for the entire day.

42
00:03:17,220 --> 00:03:22,060
And after that, you'll fill the hole back up and repeat for a whole week.

43
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:25,820
Woo-hoo!

44
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,080
The hot springs with my big brother.

45
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:31,200
We've had word from headquarters.

46
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:36,320
It's come to my attention that supplementary personnel are currently being deployed from DEM.

47
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:40,860
And unlike you and your platoon, they've managed to figure out a way to use magic correctly.

48
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,880
Not that I think for a moment you would lose to civilian transfers.

49
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,180
Far from it.

50
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:49,680
But there's nothing wrong with observing their technique, right?

51
00:03:50,940 --> 00:03:52,060
Roger that, sir.

52
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,800
Um, excuse me, captain.

53
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:01,780
What is it?

54
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,100
I wanted to ask about the company trip this weekend.

55
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:06,900
Oh, you mean the 13 Secret Hot Springs Tour?

56
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:09,700
With all-you-can-eat delicacies from different regions?

57
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:10,880
Yeah, about that.

58
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:14,680
So you know how more spirits have been turning up lately?

59
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:18,000
Well, our alert levels have increased a tiny bit.

60
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:21,260
What are you saying?

61
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:25,440
Well, I'm sorry, but the trip has been canceled.

62
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,260
Screw you!

63
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:29,600
Spirits!

64
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:30,920
Now, hold on.

65
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,540
Please, let me finish.

66
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:32,880
Huh?

67
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:39,660
I know it won't replace the trip, but the troops and I were thinking, why don't we send you to Tengu Paradise Hot Springs?

68
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:41,560
You deserve some kind of break.

69
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:44,740
I think a day of relaxation is exactly what you need right now.

70
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,020
It's our way of saying thanks for everything.

71
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,540
Plus, it's already handled, so you have to go.

72
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:55,800
Thank you.

73
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:56,740
Very nice work.

74
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:59,100
I think you just earned a double rank position.

75
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,800
Okay, but I'm not dead.

76
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:07,240
I can't wait to go.

77
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:09,160
I love the hot springs.

78
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,780
Best day ever.

79
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:15,400
Listen up!

80
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,280
The captain has accepted our invitation.

81
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,320
Hot springs are fast!

82
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,040
I do not approve.

83
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:31,740
This is time that you could be using to train and add power to the team.

84
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,680
One day?

85
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:42,620
Hello, Shido.

86
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:43,920
Hey, what's up?

87
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:47,100
Can I return the book I borrowed from you sometime tomorrow?

88
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,740
Of course, that's fine.

89
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:49,700
Bye-bye.

90
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:52,100
Uh, something happened.

91
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,940
Come on, Shido, let's go!

92
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,200
A hot springs paradise!

93
00:05:55,440 --> 00:05:57,260
Okay, you have to stop pulling my shirt!

94
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:58,260
Sorry, Origami.

95
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,080
I'll talk to you later.

96
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,240
Whoa, she's mad!

97
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:07,640
Oh, my God, man.

98
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:18,700
Oh, wow, this is so neat!

99
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:20,260
Hey, that's right.

100
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,520
I forgot this is the first car ride for you two.

101
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,480
It's pretty cool, isn't it?

102
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:28,000
Just be careful not to get carsick.

103
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,140
Oh, pet me, too.

104
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:32,700
Oh.

105
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,800
I don't think I can reach that far.

106
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,320
It's not fair for you to touch her like that and not me.

107
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:41,120
Come on.

108
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,800
You're the one who said you wanted to sit in the front seat.

109
00:06:44,220 --> 00:06:45,760
Oh, yeah.

110
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,700
Look, Shido, I'm in front of you.

111
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,980
Pet me, too.

112
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:50,200
Okay.

113
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,700
Who's a cute rat?

114
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:55,980
Oh, Shido, what's that spinner thing?

115
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:57,620
Oh, that?

116
00:06:58,060 --> 00:06:59,120
That's a barber pole.

117
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:01,440
Hey, what about that?

118
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,700
I think it's one of those laundry flanks.

119
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:05,300
Mom, I'm a dad!

120
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:23,780
Okay, if you say so.

121
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:27,240
I never dreamed we would be using the deployment train to take a day trip.

122
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:28,780
Let's not lose track here.

123
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:32,960
Our goal is to confirm the operation of the vehicle.

124
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:35,920
We're making a periodic check of a route we don't normally use.

125
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:36,760
It's not for fun.

126
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:39,480
So stop messing around and come to order, troops.

127
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:40,880
She's having fun.

128
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:41,980
She's messing around.

129
00:07:42,760 --> 00:07:43,240
Agreed.

130
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:44,260
The captain's right.

131
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:48,440
If we're going to the hot springs, we need to be well prepared.

132
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:50,700
We must document this rare outing.

133
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:51,840
Hot springs?

134
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:52,560
Hot springs?

135
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:53,680
Hot springs.

136
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:54,180
Hot springs.

137
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:03,960
The hell was that?

138
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,040
I'll check!

139
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,520
What is going on out here?

140
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:09,660
Oh.

141
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:10,780
Really?

142
00:08:11,380 --> 00:08:11,900
Okay.

143
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,340
The tunnel caved in, so there's an emergency shutdown.

144
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:17,580
They don't know yet when the service will be restored.

145
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:20,960
Nothing we can do about it now.

146
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:21,620
Troops?

147
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:22,180
Ma'am!

148
00:08:22,400 --> 00:08:24,960
They leave us no choice but to march to our location.

149
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:25,680
Forward!

150
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:26,320
Roger!

151
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:37,200
Will you please forgive me?

152
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:41,220
That was so cool, Toka!

153
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:43,440
You broke the entire car just by using...

154
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:53,720
Cheer up.

155
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:54,660
It's going to be okay.

156
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:57,680
Does that mean you're not mad anymore?

157
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,880
No, I'm not mad at all.

158
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:27,460
Several unknowns are turning up on the radar.

159
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:28,940
Confirmation needed.

160
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,500
They have been matched.

161
00:09:32,820 --> 00:09:33,540
It's the AST.

162
00:09:34,080 --> 00:09:34,660
The AST?

163
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:36,440
What are they doing here?

164
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:37,780
That's strange.

165
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,100
Maybe it's because of the spirits?

166
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,420
I highly doubt it.

167
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:43,640
They aren't even able to detect spirit waves from Toka and the others right now.

168
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,840
Don't worry about why.

169
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:47,960
Any contact we make now could interfere with the plan.

170
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:49,780
Sound the emergency code.

171
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:50,700
We should wait.

172
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:52,360
The commander's out on business.

173
00:09:52,940 --> 00:09:55,260
And our second-in-command is busy with this punishment.

174
00:09:55,560 --> 00:09:55,980
Enough!

175
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:58,720
According to Article 22, Clause 3,

176
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:01,700
if there's an emergency, we have the right to transfer command.

177
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:05,560
If at least five crew members agree, we can sound the code.

178
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,780
Dove, hands on sounding the code!

179
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:14,960
Confirm!

180
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:18,700
I, Bat-Marriage, Kuwagaway, temporarily accept the role of deputy commander.

181
00:10:19,420 --> 00:10:19,900
Yes!

182
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,280
Deputy commander?

183
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:23,240
I like the sound of that.

184
00:10:23,780 --> 00:10:25,000
Activate the code!

185
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:27,260
Form the absolute defense line!

186
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,740
And prepare to attack!

187
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,460
Block the advance of the AST!

188
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:31,080
Roger!

189
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:44,220
Yep, I was right.

190
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,740
This is much different from the map.

191
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,480
That street doesn't look familiar.

192
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:48,900
Captain!

193
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,720
There's a dead end up ahead!

194
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,560
The right flank is also a dead end!

195
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:55,460
There's a shopping arcade 500 miles straight ahead of us!

196
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:56,480
Behind us!

197
00:10:56,580 --> 00:10:57,760
The street has been destroyed!

198
00:10:57,760 --> 00:11:00,000
We can't help that.

199
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:00,860
Hey, Origami.

200
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:01,420
Ma'am.

201
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:02,820
Keep watch from up above.

202
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:03,720
Roger that.

203
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:09,740
Checking.

204
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:12,140
There is no shopping arcade over to the left,

205
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:14,640
but I do see a side road a short distance ahead.

206
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,840
Looks like it connects to the main road after about a quarter of a mile.

207
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:18,840
That'll work!

208
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:20,740
Troops, forward, march!

209
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:20,960
Oh, my gosh.

210
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:32,660
Kotori, what are you doing here?

211
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:34,120
Hi!

212
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:35,460
It's so good to see you!

213
00:11:35,560 --> 00:11:35,740
Hello?

214
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,100
Is there something wrong?

215
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:38,960
No, not at all.

216
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:40,180
I was just...

217
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:42,480
I wanted to make sure that Shida was doing his job.

218
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:42,860
What?

219
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:44,560
You can do all that from the ship.

220
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:45,740
Be real.

221
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:47,960
You just wanted to come with us to the hot springs, right?

222
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,640
Don't be ridiculous.

223
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:50,940
Look, it's okay.

224
00:11:51,220 --> 00:11:52,340
Why don't we all go together?

225
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,360
It'll be a lot of fun.

226
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:55,600
Well, I guess if you insist.

227
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:56,340
Let's go.

228
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:03,260
What in the world is going on?

229
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:06,000
So, if you need anything, just let me know, okay?

230
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:07,940
Thanks, I guess, but what about you?

231
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:08,700
I said I'm fine!

232
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:10,500
I'll catch up with you later.

233
00:12:10,580 --> 00:12:10,700
Okay.

234
00:12:11,400 --> 00:12:12,280
Oh, man.

235
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:14,640
Why did something have to happen now?

236
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,700
This is starting to get ridiculous.

237
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:20,420
There was definitely a path plot here.

238
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:22,620
No reaction here.

239
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,740
Vibration and infrared sensor failed.

240
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:27,700
No reaction from the acoustic sensor either.

241
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:30,420
And no humans detected within 500 meters.

242
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:34,120
The walls around here are a minimum of 50 centimeters thick

243
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,840
and are heavily enforced with rebar.

244
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,420
Like that'll stop me!

245
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,660
Bring it here.

246
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:43,240
Right.

247
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:48,200
Troops, attention, please.

248
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:49,960
About fate!

249
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:51,040
Forward march!

250
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,140
What just happened here?

251
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:01,500
Uh-oh.

252
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:02,240
What's that?

253
00:13:02,480 --> 00:13:03,900
Did I do something just now?

254
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:04,460
No.

255
00:13:04,660 --> 00:13:05,240
You did nothing.

256
00:13:05,640 --> 00:13:07,280
The wall exploded all by itself.

257
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,400
Oh, no!

258
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:10,060
That's so scary!

259
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:11,500
Crap.

260
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:12,740
It figures.

261
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:15,500
Looks like the damn AST decided to meddle again.

262
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,800
Switch to Datetown Type 2 in combat mode.

263
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:22,140
And use whatever firearms you feel are necessary.

264
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:22,780
Commander?

265
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,140
What are you doing out there?

266
00:13:24,360 --> 00:13:25,340
The site inspection.

267
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:26,460
Don't worry about me.

268
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:27,520
Confirm your orders.

269
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:28,060
Right.

270
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:31,660
Transitioning to Datetown Type 2 in combat mode.

271
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:33,140
Eliminating the AST.

272
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:46,680
What is this?

273
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:51,200
Rose!

274
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:52,200
What is happening?

275
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:53,880
It's so cold.

276
00:13:54,260 --> 00:13:55,080
Move carefully.

277
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:56,200
This doesn't feel right.

278
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:57,300
Look alive, ladies.

279
00:13:57,580 --> 00:13:58,140
And hurry!

